# Local Windows development paths

When working on the developer's Windows machine:

| Role | Path |
|------|------|
| WordPress install (docroot) | `C:\devel\wordpress` |
| **GitHub source checkouts** | `C:\devel\wordpress\source` |
| This plugin repo | `C:\devel\wordpress\source\wp-taxonomy-tree` |
| Web server stack (Laragon/XAMPP) | outside docroot, e.g. `C:\laragon` |

## Rules

- Clone and work on GitHub sources **only** under `C:\devel\wordpress\source\<repo-name>`.
- Do **not** put git checkouts directly in `C:\devel\wordpress` root (that stays the WP install).
- When the plugin is implemented, link or deploy into `C:\devel\wordpress\wp-content\plugins\wp-taxonomy-tree` from the source checkout (junction/symlink preferred).
- Cloud agents cannot access `C:\`; give the developer the exact `git` commands for local checkout when needed.
